OpenSandbox's upstream source and dependency notices are retained in the
unmodified build checkout. This project adds source preflight, strict lifecycle
coordination, a local CLI, and portability fixtures. It is not an official
Kubernetes or OpenSandbox project.

The helper image contains an attribution bundle at
`/usr/share/licenses/sandbox-oci`. The bundle includes this project's
`LICENSE`, this `NOTICE`, `versions.json`, the pinned OpenSandbox `LICENSE`,
attribution files collected for the helper's Go dependency graph, Go and
toolchain license materials, Debian CA-certificate copyright and common
license texts, and helper build information. The dependency manifest is
`/usr/share/licenses/sandbox-oci/manifest.json`.

The attribution collector is automated and intentionally conservative. It can
include notices that are not individually applicable to every binary or
module, and it is not a complete legal determination or an SBOM. Review the
upstream terms and the files shipped in the image for distribution decisions.
